Implementing a multi-tree list within an Angular application involves creating multiple tree structures and allowing them to be navigated and interacted with together. Below is a high-level guide on how you can achieve this:

### 1. Set Up Your Project

First, ensure you have Node.js installed. Then create a new Angular project using the following command:

```bash
ng new multiTreeListApp
cd multiTreeListApp
```

### 2. Create the Tree Structures

You'll need two types of tree lists: one for each type of data (e.g., categories and subcategories).

#### Category Tree

Create a component for the category tree.

**category.component.ts**

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-category',
  templateUrl: './category.component.html'
})
export class CategoryComponent {
  // Define your categories here
  categories = [
    { id: 0, name: 'Categories', children: [
      { id: 1, name: 'SubCategoryA' },
      { id: 2, name: 'SubCategoryB' }
    ]},
    { id: 3, name: 'Other Categories'}
  ];

  // Add methods to handle tree navigation
}
```

**category.component.html**

```html
<ul>
  <li *ngFor="let cat of categories">
    {{cat.name}}
    <ul>
      <li *ngFor="let subCat of cat.children">
        {{subCat.name}}
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
```

#### Subcategory Tree

Similarly, create a component for the subcategory tree.

**subcategory.component.ts**

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-subcategory',
  templateUrl: './subcategory.component.html'
})
export class SubcategoryComponent {
  // Define your subcategories here
  subcategories = [
    { id: 1, name: 'SubCategory A', parent: 1, children: [
      { id: 11, name: 'SubSubCategory A-1'},
      { id: 12, name: 'SubSubCategory A-2'}
    ]},
    { id: 2, name: 'SubCategory B', parent: 2, children: [
      { id: 21, name: 'SubSubCategory B-1'},
      { id: 22, name: 'SubSubCategory B-2'}
    ]}
  ];

  // Add methods to handle tree navigation
}
```

**subcategory.component.html**

```html
<ul>
  <li *ngFor="let subCat of subcategories">
    {{subCat.name}} (Parent: {{subCat.parent}})
    <ul>
      <li *ngFor="let childSubCat of subCat.children">
        {{childSubCat.name}}
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
```

### 3. Bind Components to Parent Component

In your main `app.component.html` or any other page that needs both trees, you will bind these components.

**index.html**

```html
<app-category></app-category>
<app-subcategory></app-subcategory>
```

